# Radix UI & Accessibility

**When to use Radix primitives:**
- ✅ Complex interactions (dropdowns, dialogs, popovers)
- ✅ Keyboard navigation requirements
- ✅ Built-in ARIA states and focus management
- ❌ Simple semantic elements (lists, headings, divs) - use native HTML

**ARIA attributes:**
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Proper ARIA for alerts
<div role="alert" aria-live="polite">Error message</div>

// ✅ GOOD - Hidden decorative icons
<IconCheck aria-hidden="true" className="size-4" />

// ❌ BAD - Missing ARIA for custom interactive elements
<div onClick={handleClick}>Click me</div>

// ✅ GOOD - Proper button semantics
<button onClick={handleClick} aria-label="Close dialog">
  <IconX aria-hidden="true" />
</button>
```

# Component Structure

**Exports - gather at the bottom:**
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - All exports at bottom, one per line
export {
  Badge,
  badgeVariants,
};

// ❌ BAD - Exports scattered throughout file
export const Badge = () => { ... }
// ... more code ...
export const badgeVariants = cva(...)
```

**Type definitions:**
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Inline prop typing, no export
const Badge = ({ className, ...props }: ComponentProps<"div">) => { ... }

// ❌ BAD - Exported types unless needed externally
export interface BadgeProps extends ComponentProps<"div"> { ... }
export const Badge = (props: BadgeProps) => { ... }
```

# Composition Over Configuration

**Use multiple components instead of many props:**
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Composition pattern
<Card>
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle>Title</CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>Content</CardContent>
</Card>

// ❌ BAD - Single component with many props
<Card 
  title="Title"
  content="Content"
  showHeader={true}
  headerAlign="left"
/>
```

# Styling Conventions

**className merging with cn():**
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Always use cn() for className merging
const Badge = ({ className, ...props }: ComponentProps<"div">) => (
  <div className={cn("inline-flex items-center", className)} {...props} />
);

// ❌ BAD - Direct className concatenation
<div className={`inline-flex ${className}`} />
```

**data-slot attributes for CSS targeting:**
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - All components get data-slot
<div data-slot="badge" className={cn(badgeVariants({ variant }))} />
<span data-slot="avatar-fallback">{children}</span>

// ❌ BAD - No data-slot attribute
<div className={cn(badgeVariants({ variant }))} />
```

**No arbitrary Tailwind values:**
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Use design tokens
className="leading-4.5 text-sm gap-2"

// ❌ BAD - Arbitrary values
className="leading-[18px] text-[14px] gap-[8px]"
```

# Variants with CVA

**Always use class-variance-authority for variants:**
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - CVA with defaultVariants
const badgeVariants = cva(
  "inline-flex items-center rounded-md",
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        default: "bg-primary text-primary-foreground",
        secondary: "bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground",
      },
      size: {
        sm: "text-xs px-2",
        md: "text-sm px-3",
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: "default",
      size: "md",
    },
  }
);

// Export if reusable
export { badgeVariants };
```

# forwardRef Pattern

**Use forwardRef for components wrapping HTML elements:**
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - forwardRef with displayName
const Badge = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, ComponentProps<"div">>(
  ({ className, ...props }, ref) => (
    <div ref={ref} className={cn(badgeVariants(), className)} {...props} />
  )
);
Badge.displayName = "Badge";

// ✅ GOOD - Sub-components follow parent naming
const CardHeader = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, ComponentProps<"div">>(...)
CardHeader.displayName = "CardHeader";
```

# Component Naming

- ✅ Clear, descriptive names: `InlineCitation`, `MessageAvatar`
- ✅ Sub-components match parent: `Card` → `CardHeader`, `CardTitle`, `CardContent`
- ❌ Generic names that conflict: `Container`, `Wrapper`, `Box`

# File Organization

**Import order:**
```tsx
// 1. React
import { forwardRef } from "react";

// 2. Third-party
import { cva } from "class-variance-authority";
import { IconCheck } from "@tabler/icons-react";

// 3. Local utilities
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";
```

**Definition order:**
- Helper functions and contexts first
- Components in dependency order (used components before using components)
- Exports at the bottom

# Documentation

**Component documentation:**
```tsx
/**
 * Badge component for displaying labels, statuses, and tags.
 * Supports multiple variants, sizes, and decorative options.
 */
const Badge = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, BadgeProps>(...)
```

**Metadata file:**
- Create `*.metadata.ts` for component documentation
- Include usage examples, props descriptions, accessibility notes

**Storybook stories:**
- Follow `building-stories.mdc` rules
- Use `prompt-input.stories.tsx` as gold standard
- ✅ Explicit render functions, not just args
- ✅ Include order parameters, play functions, accessibility tests

# Side Navigation

**After creating a new component, add it to `src/components/side-navigation.tsx`:**

Use the component's Storybook category (from `title` in story meta) to determine placement:

```tsx
// Story meta title determines category
const meta: Meta<typeof Badge> = {
  title: "Primitives/Badge",  // → Add to primitivesNavigation
  // ...
};
```

**Navigation categories:**
- `Primitives/Colors`, `Primitives/Effects`, `Primitives/Layouts`, `Primitives/Typography` → Add to **Foundations** subsection in `primitivesNavigation`
- `Primitives/[ComponentName]` → Add to **Primitives** subsection in `primitivesNavigation` (alphabetically)
- `AI/[ComponentName]` → Add to **AI Chat** subsection in `aiNavigation` (alphabetically)
- `Patterns/[PatternName]` → Add to **Patterns** subsection in `patternsNavigation`

**Example:**
```tsx
// Adding a new primitive component
const primitivesNavigation: NavigationItem[] = [
  {
    href: "#",
    label: "Primitives",
    isSubsection: true,
    children: [
      { href: "/primitives/accordion", label: "Accordion" },
      { href: "/primitives/alert", label: "Alert" },
      { href: "/primitives/badge", label: "Badge" }, // ← New component
      // ... rest alphabetically
    ],
  },
];
```

# Registry

**After creating/updating components:**
1. Component is auto-discovered from filesystem (no manual registry needed)
2. Run `pnpm run registry:build` to generate public JSON files
3. Verify `public/r/*.json` files are generated

# Code Quality Checklist

- ✅ No linter errors (run before committing)
- ✅ Type safety - avoid `any`, use proper TypeScript
- ✅ Prop spreading with `...props` for flexibility
- ✅ Use `ComponentProps<typeof X>` for wrapping components
- ✅ Consistent patterns - similar components should look similar
- ✅ Accessibility - ARIA labels, keyboard navigation, focus management
- ✅ Side navigation updated with new component in correct category
